== ψ Implementation ==

=== TPMS Waveguide Channel Architecture ===

A ψ waveguide is a TPMS channel with:
* '''Cross-section:''' typically rectangular or circular, chosen to support single-mode operation at the operating frequency
* '''Wall material:''' high-<math>\mu_\psi</math> ferrofluid-saturated composite (Neumann-approximating) on all transverse faces
* '''Fill:''' same BST-PZT-quartz composite as resonator, tuned for low loss tangent to minimise propagation loss
* '''Length:''' determined by PsiNet topology; not constrained by resonance (waveguide ≠ resonator)

=== Single-Mode Design Criterion ===

For [[PsiNet]] applications, single-mode operation is preferred — mode mixing at bends and junctions produces crosstalk. Single-mode condition: operate above ψ₁₀ cutoff but below ψ₂₀ cutoff:

:<math>\omega_c^{(10)} < \omega < \omega_c^{(20)}</math>

:<math>\sqrt{m_{\rm eff}^2 + \frac{\pi^2}{a^2}} < \omega < \sqrt{m_{\rm eff}^2 + \frac{4\pi^2}{a^2}}</math>

This gives a single-mode bandwidth:

:<math>\Delta\omega_{\rm SM} = \sqrt{m_{\rm eff}^2 + 4\pi^2/a^2} - \sqrt{m_{\rm eff}^2 + \pi^2/a^2}</math>

At the Stabilizer design point (<math>m_{\rm eff} = 5</math> m⁻¹) with channel width <math>a = 2</math> cm:

:<math>\omega_c^{(10)} = \sqrt{25 + \pi^2/0.0004} \approx \sqrt{25 + 24674} \approx 157</math> rad/s ... 

In natural units; restoring SI: <math>\omega_c^{(10)}/(2\pi) \approx 8</math> kHz, <math>\omega_c^{(20)}/(2\pi) \approx 16</math> kHz. Single-mode window: 8–16 kHz. The 40 kHz Stabilizer operating frequency is well above both — the 2 cm channel is multimode at 40 kHz. For single-mode at 40 kHz, need <math>a < 1</math> cm.

