== ψ-Dependent Extensions ==

=== Slow-Wave Structures for Delay Lines ===

Near the cutoff frequency, <math>v_g \to 0</math> and the group delay <math>t_g = L/v_g \to \infty</math>. A ψ waveguide operated just above cutoff is a slow-wave delay line — ψ pulses travel very slowly through it, accumulating phase delay. Potential application: a ψ memory buffer in PsiNet, storing a ψ pulse for a controlled duration before releasing it.

For a 1 m channel operating at <math>\omega = 1.1\,\omega_c</math>: <math>v_g = \sqrt{1 - (1/1.1)^2} \approx 0.42c</math>, delay = 8 ns. At <math>\omega = 1.01\,\omega_c</math>: <math>v_g \approx 0.14c</math>, delay = 24 ns per metre. Near-cutoff operation provides tens of nanoseconds of adjustable delay — relevant for PsiNet synchronisation protocols.

